<!--
  BLURRG_RSW_PORT_1 - Blurrg creature port (MLIE_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1 pattern, self-contained).
  Ported from mlie.starwarsanimalcollection's `Blurrg` ThingDef/PawnKindDef
  (Races_Animal_SW.xml), renamed under the RSW_ tier prefix. This one file carries
  everything the port needs that was not already absorbed: the BodyDef (RSW_Blurrg),
  the two eggs (RSW_EggBlurrg{,Un}Fertilized), the ThingDef and the PawnKindDef.
  Already-absorbed parts are referenced, not redefined: RSW_SW_Club, RSW_SW_Claw,
  RSW_SWTailAttackTool, RSW_SWLeft/RightArmClawAttackTool (RSW_MlieWaveB_BodyParts.xml),
  RSW_SW_Spur (RSW_MlieWaveB_Abilities.xml), RSW_Leather_Saurian / RSW_Saurian_Meat
  (RSW_MlieWaveB_Resources.xml), RSW_Pawn_Blurrg_* (SoundDefs_SWBestiary.xml).

  TAMED-ONLY (ruling: leaningscrub_bedazzle_cast_2026-09-29.md section 8). There is NO
  <wildBiomes> block - the donor's five biome rows were dropped - and this def must
  never be added to any biome <wildAnimals> roster. It arrives by trade, scenario or
  quest. The donor's trainability None became Advanced so it can actually be tamed and
  trained (specialTrainables carries the Odyssey spur, as the Dewback does).

  Values baked in, because the campaign patches that normalised the donor def key on
  the donor defName `Blurrg` and never touch this one: BeastNorm_Law3.xml (bite power
  37.5 / cooldown 2.37, manhunterOnDamageChance 0.9, manhunterOnTameFailChance 0.4) and
  MegafaunaYield.xml (MeatAmount 350). BoneAmount 125 is NOT baked - it is a modded
  StatDef and belongs in the generated doctrine patch, not in a def.

  Mount sizing, scaled from vanilla Dromedary (MoveSpeed 4.3, MarketValue 300,
  CaravanRidingSpeedFactor 1.3, bodySize 2.1, healthScale 1.6): the blurrg is the faster,
  heavier, meaner animal - donor MoveSpeed 5.0 / MarketValue 700, bodySize 2.5, healthScale
  3.5, CaravanRidingSpeedFactor 1.5 (canon: outran AT-RTs; Dromedary 1.3 is the vanilla mount).

  ART IS BLOCKED. texPath Things/Pawn/Animal/RSW_Blurrg/RSW_Blurrg is wired
  (Graphic_Multi, _south/_east/_north) but the PNGs do not exist yet; the artpipe jobs
  rsw_blurrg_v1_{south,east,north} are queued and pending. Drop-in path:
  src/RimStarWars/SWBestiary/Textures/Things/Pawn/Animal/RSW_Blurrg/. The donor's art lives
  in its AssetBundle and is deliberately not reused. Canon: design/RimStarWars/canon_references/blurrg/
  (canon gives the blurrg two short clawed arms - the body below keeps them).
-->
